h-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787295619180130001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fd653788-54f9-4c43-8860-f73146d2ed8d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d319-a094-4ee7-4549"}],"description":"## Problem\nFound during the Step 7 parity census of bug `dystopian-bardlike-basil` (d319-a094-4ee7-4549).\n\n`.github/complexity-baseline.README.md` §\"Updating the baseline (draining stale debt)\" says:\n\n> To remove stale entries or lower ceilings **after refactoring**, run:\n> `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --update-stale`\n\nThat reads as an instruction to the contributor who just refactored. `AGENTS.md` says the\nopposite — `--lock`/`--update-stale` are \"maintenance-only, not a contributor's escape hatch\".\n\n## Why it is a doc-parity gap, not the same defect\nThis is NOT what caused the local/CI split in d319 (that was three tree-scoped assertions in\n`tests/unit/test_complexity_baseline.py`, fixed there). Both statements are individually true:\nthe CI `--lock` step genuinely allows lowered ceilings and removed entries to pass freely, so a\ncontributor CAN commit a drained baseline. The gap is that two docs give a contributor opposite\nadvice about whether they SHOULD.\n\nd319 settled the sanctioned path as \"land the improvement and change nothing; the stale entry\ndrains later under maintenance\", and recorded that in AGENTS.md. The README should be made\nconsistent with it — scope the `--update-stale` recipe explicitly to maintenance, and point the\npost-refactor contributor at the do-nothing path.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.github/complexity-baseline.README.md` no longer frames `--update-stale` as a routine\n      post-refactor contributor step.\n- [ ] The README states the contributor path for a legitimate complexity reduction (land it, do\n      not edit the baseline), consistent with AGENTS.md.\n- [ ] No change to the gate scripts or to `.github/complexity-baseline.json`.\n\n## Out of scope\nThe three assertions fixed under d319. This is documentation only.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".github/complexity-baseline.README.md","reason":"Scope the --update-stale recipe to maintenance and state the contributor path."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0740-8c81-cf58-4edc","ticket_type":"task","title":"Baseline README presents --update-stale as a post-refactor contributor step, contradicting AGENTS.md's maintenance-only rule","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a8d32daf-f6c0-4d9c-babd-2802a8aecac4","6310bca1-176f-4fd8-9542-1626000e7d35","fd653788-54f9-4c43-8860-f73146d2ed8d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787299813688284001,"uuid":"b029b019-8df2-4c8d-98d7-0c45d56a869a"}